Refactor uninstall.sh: Add selective removal modes and improve safety

    Major Changes:
    - Add three uninstall modes: single (-d), all (--all), and purge (--purge)
      * -d NUM: Remove single installation, preserve Docker/Caddy
      * --all: Remove all 3X-UI installations, preserve Docker/Caddy
      * --purge: Complete removal including Docker/Caddy
    - Implement selective Caddyfile domain removal using AWK
    - Add automatic Caddy service reload after configuration changes

    New Functions:
    - detect_install_dir(): Smart directory detection with PID support
    - get_all_dirs(): Retrieve all installation directories
    - remove_caddy_config(): Surgically remove domain-specific config from Caddyfile
    - remove_single_installation(): Targeted removal without affecting shared services
    - remove_all_installations(): Batch removal preserving Docker/Caddy
    - purge_everything(): Complete system cleanup

    Bug Fixes:
    - Fix undefined variable $dir in list_directories() single directory case
    - Add proper null checks for domain name and file existence
    - Add stderr redirection (2>/dev/null) to grep commands
    - Fix string comparison quotes in conditional statements
    - Improve error handling with graceful fallbacks

    Improvements:
    - Better argument parsing with proper shift handling
    - Enhanced list_directories() with container status and domain info
    - Consistent output formatting across all modes
    - Add Caddyfile existence check before modification
    - Validate domain name extraction before processing

    This refactor prevents uninstall from breaking other panels that depend on
    Docker/Caddy by providing granular control over what gets removed.
